                    {
                        "sense_id": "2b51d12c-90cd-3213-a633-7fbe743e419f",
                        "entry_id": "c86779e2-49a5-35f0-8b12-635d36b17680",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A valley in Yanggu, Gangwon Province, South Korea."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a38b5211-8d10-4a9d-b2ca-703acce30c2d",
                                "sense_id": "2b51d12c-90cd-3213-a633-7fbe743e419f",
                                "text": "Hill 930 here, about 100 miles northeast of Seoul, just above the village of Wontong, towers over a region still called the Punchbowl because that is what it looked like to G.I.'s during the Korean War.[…]\n\"The Korean War is to all accounts and purposes ignored,\" said Rudy Basurto of Lompoc, Calif., who was a medic with the 45th Division 33 years ago in the Punchbowl."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52abbc6e-da7b-445f-acb9-b56aa064207c",
                                "sense_id": "2b51d12c-90cd-3213-a633-7fbe743e419f",
                                "text": "Naimo ran to their aid, exposing himself to withering enemy mortar, artillery and machine gun fire sweeping his company’s position: Hill 1052, near what would be called “The Punchbowl,” north of the 38th Parallel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8e03893-2d83-46ea-b417-3f6b6c7d39c8",
                                "sense_id": "2b51d12c-90cd-3213-a633-7fbe743e419f",
                                "text": "Our drive north brings us to Haean-myeon valley, a highland basin in the far northeast of South Korea, and which was nicknamed “the punchbowl” by American-led United Nations forces during the Korean war. Jung, KFS biologist Bak Gippeum and I stroll through the 375-acre National DMZ Botanical Garden, which opened four years ago."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
